Apple's rumored "iPhone 20 Pro" could return to titanium as part of a more rounded design, according to the leaker known as "<a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/fixed-focus-digital/">Fixed Focus Digital</a>."<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/11/Titanium-iPhone-15-Pro.jpg" alt="" width="2000" height="1000" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1078198" /><br/>
In a <a href="https://weibo.com/5821279480/5366713626657738">new post on Weibo</a>, the leaker said the iPhone 20 Pro will adopt a titanium frame with a more rounded design. A frame made of titanium is reportedly currently in use on prototype devices during early engineering work. They described the design as somewhat similar to the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/iphone-air/">iPhone Air</a>, but substantially more rounded. <br/>
<br/>
If the claim proves accurate, it would mark a return to titanium for the Pro lineup. Apple used titanium frames for the iPhone 15 Pro and <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/iphone-16/">iPhone 16</a> Pro, before <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2025/09/10/IPHONE-17-PRO-HANDS-ON/">switching to an aluminum unibody design</a> with the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/iphone-17/">iPhone 17</a> Pro in 2025. Apple highlighted aluminum's thermal conductivity as part of that redesign, which also introduced a vapor chamber to improve sustained performance.<br/>
<br/>
While the change was praised for its improved thermals, light weight, and distinctive design, some users missed the more premium look and feel of titanium, along with its superior resistance to damage. The latest report regards development hardware, so it is still open whether titanium will be used in the finished product, but it seems plausible. The &zwnj;iPhone Air&zwnj; and <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/iphone-duo/">iPhone Duo</a> continue to use titanium frames.<br/>
<br/>
The leaker's comparison with the &zwnj;iPhone Air&zwnj; builds on earlier claims about how Apple is developing the anniversary models. Earlier this week, Fixed Focus Digital said the devices would <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/11/16/iphone-20-pro-to-be-based-on-iphone-air/">use the same glass</a> material as the &zwnj;iPhone Air&zwnj;, reshaped with greater curvature along all four sides.<br/>
<br/>
An illustration accompanying that post depicted curved front and rear glass meeting a narrow, polished metal frame. In August, Fixed Focus Digital claimed that Apple had <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/08/24/iphone-20-curved-glass-to-be-like-iphone-air/">modified iPhone Air manufacturing equipment</a> to produce the more rounded glass components.<br/>
<br/>
That combination of curved glass and a narrow metal frame is consistent with <em>Bloomberg</em>'s <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/mark-gurman/">Mark Gurman</a>'s reporting that Apple is planning front and rear glass panels that <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/08/10/glass-centric-iphone-still-planned-2027/">curve into the sides around a thin metal band</a>. Gurman said an earlier, more ambitious version that replaced even more metal with glass had been abandoned during development.<br/>
<br/>
The latest claim suggests titanium could form that remaining band. Gurman <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/09/04/iphone-20-biggest-revamp-since-iphone-x/">described</a> the planned changes as the biggest overhaul of the Pro line since the iPhone X.<br/>
<br/>
The extent of the curvature may still be under consideration. The leaker "Ice Universe" today claimed that Apple is developing <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/11/18/two-designs-for-20th-anniversary-iphone/">four models with two different designs</a>, including two with flat glass and two with glass that curves along all four edges. Apple has reportedly explored the curved design for three years, reducing the more pronounced curvature of earlier versions.<br/>
<br/>
The curved models are said to have borders measuring around 1mm, with the surrounding glass making them appear almost invisible when viewed head-on. Screen protector samples <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/11/17/iphone-20-pro-screen-protectors-rumored-design/">circulating online</a> offer a physical illustration of that approach, showing rounded corners, shallow curves along all four edges, and very narrow borders. <br/>
<br/>
Alongside the changes to the glass and frame, the displays could grow slightly. The leaker "Digital Chat Station" has claimed that the Pro and Pro Max models will feature <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/09/21/iphone-20-pro-display-sizes-leak/">6.41-inch and 6.96-inch screens</a>, respectively, while also describing a four-sided curved design intended to appear borderless.<br/>
<br/>
Separately, Ice Universe suggested that the main camera could gain a sensor with logic circuitry manufactured <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/11/16/iphone-20-pro-new-17nm-camera-sensor/">using a 17-nanometer process</a>, potentially enabling faster readout speeds and improved power efficiency. The device could also <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/11/06/apple-rumored-to-drop-the-action-button/">lose the Action button</a> and feature the "A21 Pro" chip based on TSMC's enhanced 2nm process (N2P).<br/>
<br/>
